      "publication_date": "2024-01-01",
      "abstract": "This article traces the similarities and differences between Gy\u00f6rgy Luk\u00e1cs\u2019s work The theory of the novel and Ren\u00e9 Girard's Mensonge romantique et v\u00e9rit\u00e9 romanesque, delving into the use that both thinkers make of the Western novelistic tradition to think about modernity. Two shared interpretative gestures are highlighted as crucial: the selection of a small list of novelists in whom the essence of that time is encoded, and the conceptualisation of Dostoyevsky's work as a borderline case in which the novel merges with other forms of expression. It concludes by highlighting the political weight of the essays analysed, which are a rich meditation on modern society in which aesthetic reflection, philosophy and politics are interwoven.",
